  "question": {
    "text": "A total of $48 \\mathrm{~J}$ heat is given to one mole of helium kept in a cylinder. The temperature of helium increases by $2^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The work done by the gas is:\nGiven, $\\mathrm{R}=8.3 \\mathrm{~J} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4uXTu",
      "text": "$24.9 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1Vm0X",
      "text": "$72.9 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fBzLw",
      "text": "$48 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SBBiN",
      "text": "$23.1 \\mathrm{~J}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$1^{\\text {st }}$ law of thermodynamics\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{Q}=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}+\\mathrm{W} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow+48=\\mathrm{nC}_{\\mathrm{v}} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}+\\mathrm{W} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 48=(1)\\left(\\frac{3 \\mathrm{R}}{2}\\right)(2)+\\mathrm{W} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{W}=48-3 \\times \\mathrm{R} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{W}=48-3 \\times(8.3) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{W}=23.1 \\text { Joule }\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
